A||N||7||Predator||New tach in 85 GT from 87 GT||||5||
Z||000000||Predator||07-20-2000||11:19 PM||||Hey, <BR>I got a 1985 Fiero GT with the 85 mph guage cluster. I bought a 120 mph guage cluster from a person and I have installed it. Everything pluged right in and I got the instructions for the odometer from this form. Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The problem is that the Tach goes to 2000 RPM when I crank the car and doesn't move. Is there a incompatibility between the 85 and 87 tachometers? Any direction will be appreciated. Also I got the guage pod with the oil presure guage and volt guage. I also got the instructions to splice it into my wiring harnes from this site. Thanks again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The problem with it is the volt guage works fine but the oil presure guage does not work. The oil light comes on, and the guage reads next to nothing. When I turn the headlights on it goes all the way to the right and buries itself. Any help will be appreciated. I would really like to get these guages working. They light up at night much better than the original ones. Thanks. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DJRice||07-21-2000||09:36 AM||||If you did not have the optional gauge kit, but just added the gauges, then your going to have to change the oil pressure sending unit, I think.  <P>In your cars original cluster, did it have the oil PSI gauge co-located with the tach?<P>If so, when you replace the oil pressure sending unit, the problem may straighten itself out.  Jut unplug the optional gauges and see if the tach runs normally.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Predator||07-21-2000||09:45 AM||||When you say I need to replace the oil sending unit do you mean with a 87 GT model oil sending unit? Also yes my tach did have the oil presure guage on it. I disconnected the guage pod from the tach wiring harness and the tach still stayed peged on 2000. IT moves slightly when I rev the engine but that is all. Thanks for your reply. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Predator||07-21-2000||02:15 PM||||I got the Tach working and all the instruments are in and working  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>There is one thing. The Oil Presure guage on the pod reads right, but it is eratic. It will give the correct reading that the old guage did, but it shakes a lot. Are there any remedies for this? Thanks in advance. ||||reg||7
Z||000004||80's BOY||07-21-2000||02:38 PM||||how did you get the tach working? i'm doing the same swap and don't want to see any problems. thanks in advance.<P>85 GT 3.1<BR>Texas Targa Project||||reg||5
Z||000005||Predator||07-21-2000||04:51 PM||||Well it's kind of hard to explain. It looks like the tach got shaken lose in transit to my house. I ended up taking all the guages out of the 87 board and putting them in my 85 board. The 87 came out of a auto so the lights were different. The shift for instance wasn't there. I had to place the tach in twice dur to it having to fit just right in the metal holders for it to get a good connection. Once I did that and reinstalled it it worked fine. Any ideas on fixing a shaky oil preasure gauge would be appreciated. ||||reg||3
Z||000006||Monkeyman||07-21-2000||09:10 PM||||You just might have to replace the oil sending unit for the oil pressure gauge to work right.  I've done the same thing as you have and I have the same problem.  It's common.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Predator||07-22-2000||01:53 PM||||I hate to sound stupid here, but when you suggest for me to replace the oil sending unit do you mean for me to get a 87 GT sedning unit? The Oil presure guage that was in my tach before I replaced the guages did not have any problems so I would think the oil presure sending unit is ok. Is the oil sending unit in a 87 different?||||reg||5
